.TH FLUXLAND-INIT 5 "2026-10-25" "fluxland 2.0.0" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
fluxland-init \- main configuration file for fluxland
.SH DESCRIPTION
The init file is the main configuration file for
.BR fluxland (1).
It uses X resource database syntax (key: value) to control workspaces,
focus policy, window placement, toolbar behavior, keyboard layout, and
paths to other configuration files.
.PP
By default, the file is located at
.I ~/.config/fluxland/init
within the configuration directory (or
.I ~/.fluxbox/init
when fluxland uses a Fluxbox configuration directory).
Key names are not case sensitive, so the spellings Fluxbox writes
.RB ( showwindowposition )
and its manual uses
.RB ( showWindowPosition )
both work.
A Fluxbox init file works as it is;
.B fluxland \-\-check\-config
names the keys fluxland doesn't support yet and ignores those that have
no meaning on Wayland (colorsPerChannel, cacheMax...).
Boolean values accept
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
or
.BR 1 / 0 .
.SH SYNTAX
Each line has the form:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
\fIkey\fP: \fIvalue\fP
.fi
.RE
.PP
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
or
.B !
are comments.
.SH WORKSPACE SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.workspaces
Number of workspaces (1\-32, default: 4).
.TP
.B session.screen0.workspaceNames
Comma-separated workspace names (e.g.\&
.IR Web,Code,Term,Chat ).
.TP
.B session.screen0.workspacewarping
Allow moving windows between workspaces by dragging them to the edges
of the screen, within
.B edgeSnapThreshold
of them (default: true).
An opaque move takes the window along, a wireframe one sends it when
it is let go.
.TP
.BR session.screen0.workspacewarpinghorizontal ", " session.screen0.workspacewarpingvertical
Warp at the left and right, or top and bottom edges (default: true).
.TP
.BR session.screen0.workspacewarpinghorizontaloffset ", " session.screen0.workspacewarpingverticaloffset
How many workspaces a warp goes (default: 1).
.TP
.B session.screen0.workspaceMode
Workspace mode:
.BR global " (default)"
or
.BR per-output .
.SH FOCUS SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.focusModel
Focus policy.
One of
.BR ClickToFocus " (default),"
.BR MouseFocus " (sloppy),"
or
.BR StrictMouseFocus .
.TP
.B session.screen0.autoRaise
With MouseFocus, raise the window the pointer focuses (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.focusSameHead
When the focused window goes away (or another workspace is shown), the
focus goes to a window on the head the pointer is on (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.demandsAttentionTimeout
A window that wants attention (one refused the focus, or urgent) flashes
as focused in its frame and the iconbar every this many milliseconds
until it has the focus (default: 500; 0, it doesn't flash).
.TP
.B session.screen0.tooltipDelay
After this many milliseconds over an iconbar entry or a tab whose title
is cut short, the whole title shows over the pointer (default: 500; 0
at once, \-1 never).
.TP
.B session.screen0.noFocusWhileTypingDelay
A new window doesn't take the focus from the window you typed in less
than this many milliseconds ago (Return doesn't count); it shows that
it wants attention instead (default: 0, off).
.TP
.B session.autoRaiseDelay
Delay in milliseconds before auto-raising (default: 250).
.TP
.B session.screen0.clickRaises
Clicking a window raises it (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.focusNewWindows
New windows receive focus (default: true).
.SH WINDOW BEHAVIOR
.TP
.B session.screen0.opaqueMove
Show window contents while moving (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.opaqueResize
Show window contents while resizing (default: false).
.TP
.B session.ignoreBorder
Dragging a window's border doesn't move it (Move bindings on
.B OnWindowBorder
don't start; default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.edgeSnapThreshold
Pixel distance for edge snapping (default: 10).
.TP
.B session.screen0.windowPlacement
Window placement algorithm.
One of
.BR RowSmartPlacement " (default),"
.BR ColSmartPlacement ,
.BR CascadePlacement ,
.BR UnderMousePlacement ,
.BR RowMinOverlapPlacement ,
.BR ColMinOverlapPlacement ,
or
.BR AutotabPlacement :
a tab of the focused window.
.TP
.B session.screen0.rowPlacementDirection
Direction for row placement.
One of
.BR LeftToRight " (default)"
or
.BR RightToLeft .
.TP
.B session.screen0.colPlacementDirection
Direction for column placement.
One of
.BR TopToBottom " (default)"
or
.BR BottomToTop .
.TP
.B session.screen0.maxIgnoreIncrement
A maximized window fills the screen even if that isn't a whole number
of its steps (a terminal's character cells); false keeps it to them
(default: true).
Resizing with the mouse always keeps to them.
.TP
.B session.screen0.fullMaximization
Maximize windows over the toolbar and slit (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.showWindowPosition
Show window position overlay during move/resize (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.defaultDeco
Default decoration preset for new windows (e.g.\&
.BR NORMAL ,
.BR NONE ,
.BR BORDER ).
.TP
.B session.screen0.struts
Space kept free at the edges of every head:
.IR "left, right, top, bottom"
in pixels (commas or spaces; default: 0,0,0,0).
Maximized and placed windows stay out of it.
.TP
.BI session.screen0.struts. N
The same for head
.I N
only (from 1).
.SH WINDOW OPACITY
.TP
.B session.screen0.window.focus.alpha
Opacity for focused windows (0\-255, default: 255).
.TP
.B session.screen0.window.unfocus.alpha
Opacity for unfocused windows (0\-255, default: 255).
.SH WINDOW ANIMATIONS
.TP
.B session.screen0.animateWindowMap
Fade-in animation when windows appear (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.animateWindowUnmap
Fade-out animation when windows close (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.animateMinimize
Animate minimize/restore (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.animationDuration
Animation duration in milliseconds (0\-5000, default: 300).
.SH WINDOW SNAP ZONES
.TP
.B session.screen0.enableWindowSnapping
Enable edge/corner snap zones for tiling (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.snapZoneThreshold
Pixel distance from screen edge to trigger snap zones (1\-100, default: 10).
.TP
.B session.screen0.edgeResizeSnapThreshold
A corner dragged in a resize snaps to the edges of the heads and the
other windows within this many pixels (default: 0, off).
.B edgeSnapThreshold
does the same for moves: the nearest edge the window is beside wins.
.SH TOOLBAR SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.visible
Show the toolbar (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.placement
Toolbar position.
One of
.BR TopLeft ,
.BR TopCenter ,
.BR TopRight ,
.BR BottomLeft ,
.BR BottomCenter " (default),"
.BR BottomRight ,
or up a side:
.BR LeftTop ,
.BR LeftCenter ,
.BR LeftBottom
(reading upwards),
.BR RightTop ,
.BR RightCenter ,
.BR RightBottom
(reading downwards); then
.B widthPercent
is of the screen's height.
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.autoHide
Auto-hide the toolbar (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.autoHideDelay
Delay in milliseconds before hiding (default: 500).
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.autoRaise
Bring the toolbar above the windows while the pointer is on it
(default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.widthPercent
Toolbar width as percentage of screen (10\-100, default: 100).
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.height
Toolbar height in pixels (0 = auto from font, default: 0).
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.layer
Toolbar stacking layer: a Fluxbox layer name or number;
.BR Menu " and " AboveDock
put it above windows,
.BR Dock ", " Top " and " Normal
(the default:
.BR Dock )
in the top layer,
.BR Bottom " and " Desktop
below windows.
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.alpha
Toolbar opacity (0\-255, default: 255).
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.onhead
Head (monitor) the toolbar is on, numbered from 1 as in Fluxbox;
0 or a missing head means head 1 (default: 0). See
.BR OUTPUTS .
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.tools
The toolbar's tools, separated by commas (as Fluxbox writes them) or
spaces:
.BR prevworkspace ,
.BR workspacename ,
.BR nextworkspace ,
.BR iconbar ,
.BR clock ,
.BR prevwindow ,
.BR nextwindow ,
.B systemtray
(after the other tools when it isn't listed),
.B spacer
(sharing the width left over with the iconbar),
.BI spacer_ N
.RI ( N
pixels), and
.BI button. NAME\fR,
a button with the label of
.BI session.screen0.toolbar.button. NAME .label
and the commands of
.BI session.screen0.toolbar.button. NAME .commands\fR,
one for each mouse button separated by
.B :
(the first for the left button, the second for the middle one, the
third for the right one).
Default:
.IR "workspacename prevworkspace nextworkspace iconbar clock" .
.IP
Clicks on the toolbar are Fluxbox's: on the workspace name the left
button goes to the workspace before and the right one to the one
after; on an iconbar entry the left button focuses its window (or
iconifies it when focused) and the right one opens its window menu;
the middle button opens the toolbar's menu, which is also in the
.B [config]
menu.
.TP
.B session.screen0.toolbar.maxOver
Allow maximized windows to cover the toolbar (default: false).
.TP
.BR session.screen0.systray.pinLeft ", " session.screen0.systray.pinRight
Tray icons to keep at the left or right of the system tray, by their
id, separated by spaces or commas: the first of pinLeft leftmost, the
last of pinRight rightmost.
.SH TITLEBAR SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.titlebar.left
Space-separated list of buttons for the left side of the titlebar
(default:
.IR Stick ).
Fluxbox writes this key; its manual's
.B session.titlebar.left
works too.
.TP
.B session.screen0.titlebar.right
Space-separated list of buttons for the right side of the titlebar
(default:
.IR "Minimize Maximize Close" ;
also
.BR session.titlebar.right ).
.SH CLOCK SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.strftimeFormat
Clock format string using
.BR strftime (3)
syntax (default:
.IR %H:%M ).
.SH ICONBAR SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.iconbar.mode
The windows the iconbar shows: a window list as in
.BR fluxland-keys (5),
such as
.B {static groups} (workspace)
(the default: this workspace's windows, a tab group once, in the order
they were opened),
.B {static groups} (minimized=yes)
or
.BR none .
Fluxbox 1.0's names
.BR Workspace ,
.BR AllWindows ,
.BR Icons ,
.BR NoIcons ,
.B WorkspaceIcons
and
.B WorkspaceNoIcons
work too.
.TP
.B session.screen0.iconbar.alignment
.B Relative
(the default; also
.BR RelativeSmart )
shares the iconbar out among the windows;
.B Left
and
.B Right
give each
.B iconWidth
pixels from that side
.RB ( Center ,
from fluxland 1.x, centers them).
.TP
.B session.screen0.iconbar.iconWidth
Width of an iconbar entry when not Relative (default: 128).
.TP
.B session.screen0.iconbar.iconTextPadding
Pixels around the title in an iconbar entry, half each side (default:
10).
.TP
.B session.screen0.iconbar.usePixmap
Use pixmap textures for iconbar entries (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.iconbar.wheelMode
Mouse wheel behavior on iconbar:
.BR Screen " (default, switch workspaces)"
or
.BR Off .
.TP
.B session.screen0.iconbar.iconifiedPattern
How a minimized window's title shows in the iconbar:
.B %t
is the title (default:
.BR "( %t )" ;
fluxland 1.x's
.B %s
works too).
.SH TAB SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.tabsAttachArea
Where a tab dragged with
.B StartTabbing
joins a window:
.BR Window " (default), anywhere on it, or"
.BR Titlebar .
Dropped anywhere else, it leaves its window for where it was dropped.
.TP
.B session.screen0.autoTabPlacement
Automatically group new windows into tabs (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.tabFocusModel
Tab focus model:
.BR ClickTabFocus " (default)"
or
.BR MouseTabFocus .
.TP
.B session.screen0.tabs.intitlebar
Display tabs in the titlebar (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.tabs.usePixmap
Show the window's icon in its tab (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.tabs.maxOver
A maximized window with its tabs outside the titlebar fills the screen,
its tabs off it; by default the tabs stay on it (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.tab.placement
Where the tabs hang when they aren't in the titlebar (tabs.intitlebar:
false): Fluxbox's
.BR TopLeft " (the default),"
.BR Top ,
.BR TopRight ,
.BR BottomLeft ,
.BR Bottom ,
.BR BottomRight ,
.BR LeftTop ,
.BR Left ,
.BR LeftBottom ,
.BR RightTop ,
.BR Right
or
.BR RightBottom .
Every window has its tab then, as thick as a titlebar button; down
the sides the text reads up (left) or down (right).
.TP
.B session.screen0.tab.width
The length of an external tab (default: 64).
.TP
.B session.tabPadding
Padding between tabs in pixels (default: 0; also
.BR session.screen0.tabPadding ).
.SH SLIT SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.autoHide
Auto-hide the slit (default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.autoRaise
Bring the slit above the windows while the pointer is on it
(default: false).
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.placement
Slit position.
One of
.BR TopLeft ,
.BR TopCenter ,
.BR TopRight ,
.BR RightTop ,
.BR RightCenter " (default),"
.BR RightBottom ,
.BR BottomLeft ,
.BR BottomCenter ,
.BR BottomRight ,
.BR LeftTop ,
.BR LeftCenter ,
or
.BR LeftBottom .
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.direction
Slit layout direction:
.BR Vertical " (default)"
or
.BR Horizontal .
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.layer
Slit stacking layer, as
.B toolbar.layer
(default:
.BR Dock ).
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.onhead
Head (monitor) the slit is on, numbered from 1 as in Fluxbox;
0 or a missing head means head 1 (default: 0).
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.alpha
Slit opacity (0\-255, default: 255).
.TP
.B session.screen0.slit.maxOver
Allow maximized windows to cover the slit (default: false).
.TP
.B session.slitlistFile
Path to the slit client ordering file.
.SH MENU SETTINGS
.TP
.B session.screen0.clientMenu.usePixmap
Show windows' icons in the window lists (ClientMenu, WindowList,
[workspaces]) (default: true).
.TP
.B session.screen0.menu.alpha
Menu opacity (0\-255, default: 255).
.TP
.B session.menuSearch
Menu type-ahead search:
.BR ItemStart " (the default, as in Fluxbox: from the start of a label),"
.BR Somewhere " (anywhere in a label),"
or
.BR Nowhere " (off)."
.TP
.B session.screen0.menuDelay
Submenu hover-open delay in milliseconds (0\-5000, default: 200).
.TP
.B session.screen0.windowMenu
The window menu's file (default: the
.I windowmenu
file of the configuration directory when there is one, else a copy of
Fluxbox's; see
.BR fluxland-menu (5)).
.SH TOUCHPAD GESTURES
.TP
.B session.screen0.gestureWorkspaceSwitch
Enable three-finger swipe to switch workspaces. Default: true.
.TP
.B session.screen0.gestureOverview
Enable vertical swipe up to show window list. Default: false.
.TP
.B session.screen0.gestureWorkspaceFingers
Number of fingers required for workspace gestures (2\-5). Default: 3.
.TP
.B session.screen0.gestureSwipeThreshold
Pixel distance to trigger a swipe action (10\-1000). Default: 100.
.SH WALLPAPER
.TP
.B session.screen0.wallpaper
An image for the desktop (PNG or JPEG).
Without one, the last one the
.B SetWallpaper
command (or a menu's
.BR [wallpapers] )
set is used: it is kept in the configuration directory's
.I lastwallpaper
file, as Fluxbox's fbsetbg keeps its last one.
A style's
.B background
shows when there is neither, or when a style is chosen (as Fluxbox
does); this one always wins.
.TP
.B session.screen0.wallpaperMode
.BR Stretch " (the default),"
.BR Fill " (keep its shape and cover the output),"
.BR Fit " (keep its shape and fit inside it, fbsetbg's aspect),"
.BR Center ,
or
.BR Tile .
.TP
.B session.screen0.wallpaperColor
The color around or instead of the image, as
.BR #RRGGBB .
.TP
.BI session.screen0.workspace N .wallpaper
The wallpaper of workspace
.I N
(from 0).
.SH MISCELLANEOUS
.TP
.B session.doubleClickInterval
Double-click interval in milliseconds (50\-2000, default: 250).
.TP
.B session.screen0.rootCommand
Shell command to execute on startup (e.g.\& to set a wallpaper).
.SH MOUSE BUTTON REMAPPING
.TP
.B session.mouse.button1.map
Remap mouse button 1.
Value is one of
.BR BTN_LEFT ,
.BR BTN_MIDDLE ,
.BR BTN_RIGHT ,
.BR BTN_SIDE ,
or
.BR BTN_EXTRA .
.TP
.B session.mouse.button2.map
Remap mouse button 2.
.TP
.B session.mouse.button3.map
Remap mouse button 3.
.TP
.B session.mouse.button4.map
Remap mouse button 4.
.TP
.B session.mouse.button5.map
Remap mouse button 5.
.SH XKB KEYBOARD LAYOUT
.TP
.B session.xkb.rules
XKB rules (e.g.\&
.IR evdev ).
.TP
.B session.xkb.model
Keyboard model (e.g.\&
.IR pc105 ).
.TP
.B session.xkb.layout
Keyboard layout, comma-separated for multiple layouts (e.g.\&
.IR us,de ).
.TP
.B session.xkb.variant
Layout variant (e.g.\&
.IR ,nodeadkeys ).
.TP
.B session.xkb.options
XKB options (e.g.\&
.IR grp:alt_shift_toggle,caps:escape ).
.SH SESSION
.TP
.B session.updateActivationEnvironment
Export WAYLAND_DISPLAY, DISPLAY, XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, XDG_SESSION_TYPE
and FLUXLAND_SOCK to D-Bus and systemd user services (desktop portals,
notification daemons), and empty them again at exit:
.I auto
(default: only when not nested in another session or headless),
.I true
or
.IR false .
.PP
fluxland also sets XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=fluxland:wlroots,
XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland, QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland;xcb and
SDL_VIDEODRIVER=wayland,x11 for itself and the programs it starts,
unless they are already set.
.TP
.BR session.switch.lidClose ", " session.switch.lidOpen
Command run when the laptop lid is closed or opened, in the same
language as
.BR fluxland\-keys (5)
commands, e.g.\&
.I Exec swaylock
or
.IR "Exec wlr\-randr \-\-output eDP\-1 \-\-off" .
.TP
.BR session.switch.tabletModeOn ", " session.switch.tabletModeOff
Command run when a convertible enters or leaves tablet mode.
.SH OUTPUTS
Monitors are configured per connector name (as
.BR wlr\-randr (1)
lists them: \fIeDP\-1\fR, \fIHDMI\-A\-1\fR, \fIDP\-2\fR, ...):
.RS
.nf
session.output.\fIName\fR.\fIsetting\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Settings left out keep the monitor's preferred mode and defaults. If the
settings fail (a mode the monitor rejects), the preferred mode is used.
They are applied when the monitor is plugged in and on reconfigure;
changes made with
.BR wlr\-randr (1)
or
.BR kanshi (1)
last until then.
.PP
Heads, used by \fBonhead\fR, \fBSetHead\fR and the \fB[Head]\fR window
rule, are the enabled monitors in the order they were connected, from 1.
When a monitor is unplugged or turned off, its windows, toolbar and slit
move to the remaining ones.
.TP
.B enabled
false turns the monitor off.
.TP
.B mode
\fIwidth\fRx\fIheight\fR, optionally @\fIrate\fR (e.g.\&
.I 2560x1440@143.97
); without a rate the fastest for that size.
.TP
.B scale
Scale factor, e.g.\&
.I 1.5
(0.25\-10).
.TP
.B position
\fIx\fR,\fIy\fR in the layout, e.g.\&
.IR 1920,0 .
Monitors without a position are placed to the right of the others.
.TP
.B transform
.IR normal ", " 90 ", " 180 ", " 270 ", " flipped ", " flipped\-90 ,
.IR flipped\-180 " or " flipped\-270 .
.TP
.B adaptiveSync
Variable refresh rate (true/false).
.SH INPUT DEVICES (LIBINPUT)
Pointer settings apply to every device, to a type of device, or to one
device:
.RS
.nf
session.input.\fIsetting\fR               every device
session.input.touchpad.\fIsetting\fR      touchpads
session.input.pointer.\fIsetting\fR       other pointers (mice, trackballs)
session.input.device.\fIName\fR.\fIsetting\fR one device
.fi
.RE
.PP
A more specific scope wins, wherever it appears in the file.
.I Name
is the device name as
.BR libinput (1)
.B list-devices
shows it, with every character other than a letter or digit replaced by
.BR _ ,
so
.I SynPS/2 Synaptics TouchPad
becomes
.IR SynPS_2_Synaptics_TouchPad .
Settings a device does not support are ignored; settings left out keep
libinput's default. Changes apply on reconfigure.
.TP
.BR tap ", " tapDrag ", " tapDragLock
Tap to click, tap and drag, and drag lock (true/false; touchpads).
.TP
.B tapButtonMap
.I lrm
(one/two/three fingers = left/right/middle) or
.IR lmr .
.TP
.B naturalScroll
Content follows the fingers (true/false).
.TP
.B leftHanded
Swap the primary buttons (true/false).
.TP
.B disableWhileTyping
Ignore the touchpad while typing (true/false).
.TP
.B middleEmulation
Left and right together act as middle (true/false).
.TP
.B accelProfile
.I flat
or
.IR adaptive .
.TP
.B accelSpeed
Pointer speed from \-1.0 to 1.0.
.TP
.B scrollMethod
.IR none ", " twoFinger ", " edge
or
.I button
(scroll while holding
.BR scrollButton ).
.TP
.B scrollButton
Linux button code for button scrolling (e.g.\&
.I 274
for middle,
.I 276
for back).
.TP
.B clickMethod
.IR none ", " buttonAreas
or
.IR clickFinger .
.TP
.B sendEvents
.IR enabled ", " disabled
or
.I disabledOnExternalMouse
(touchpads).
.SH FILE PATHS
These override the default locations of other configuration files.
Absolute paths, tilde-expanded paths, and relative paths (resolved from
the config directory) are supported.
.TP
.B session.keyFile
Path to key bindings file (default:
.IR keys ).
.TP
.B session.appsFile
Path to window rules file (default:
.IR apps ).
.TP
.B session.menuFile
Path to menu file (default:
.IR menu ).
.TP
.B session.styleFile
Path to style file (default:
.IR styles/default ).
.TP
.B session.styleOverlay
Path to a style overlay file applied on top of the main style.
.SH EXAMPLES
Minimal init file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
session.screen0.workspaces: 4
session.screen0.focusModel: ClickToFocus
session.screen0.toolbar.placement: BottomCenter
.fi
.RE
.PP
Power user configuration:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
session.screen0.workspaces: 6
session.screen0.workspaceNames: Web,Code,Term,Chat,Media,Misc
session.screen0.focusModel: MouseFocus
session.screen0.autoRaise: true
session.autoRaiseDelay: 200
session.screen0.edgeSnapThreshold: 15
session.screen0.windowPlacement: RowSmartPlacement

session.screen0.toolbar.placement: BottomCenter
session.screen0.toolbar.widthPercent: 80
session.screen0.toolbar.autoHide: true
session.screen0.toolbar.alpha: 230

session.screen0.enableWindowSnapping: true
session.screen0.snapZoneThreshold: 20

session.screen0.animateWindowMap: true
session.screen0.animateWindowUnmap: true
session.screen0.animationDuration: 200

session.screen0.window.focus.alpha: 255
session.screen0.window.unfocus.alpha: 200

session.screen0.strftimeFormat: %a %H:%M
session.xkb.layout: us,de
session.xkb.options: grp:alt_shift_toggle,caps:escape
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fluxland (1),
.BR fluxland-keys (5),
.BR fluxland-apps (5),
.BR fluxland-style (5),
.BR fluxland-menu (5),
.BR fluxland-startup (5)
